<setup>

  <selectFromSequence name = "a" from = "1" to = "3" step = "1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "b" from = "4" to = "6" step = "1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "c" from = "7" to = "9" step = "1"/>

  <selectFromSequence name = "k" from = "3" to = "5" step = "1" exclude="$a $b"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "m" from = "2" to = "5" step = "1" exclude="$k $a $b"/>

  <selectFromSequence name = "P" from = "3" to = "5" step = "1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "Q" from = "-3" to = "-1" step = "1" exclude="-$P"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "R" from = "-7" to = "-4" step = "1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "S" from = "1" to = "3" step = "1"/>

  
</setup>

<p>
    Let <m>f(x)</m> and <m>g(x)</m> be continuous functions on the interval <m>[$a,$c]</m>.  Use the following information along with properties of the definite integral to determine the numerical value of each integral stated below.
</p>

<tabular>
  <row>
    <cell><m>\displaystyle \int_{$a}^{$b} f(x) \, dx = $P</m></cell>
    <cell><m>\displaystyle \int_{$b}^{$c} f(x) \, dx = $Q</m></cell>
  </row>
  <row>
    <cell><m>\displaystyle \int_{$a}^{$b} g(x) \, dx = $R</m></cell>
    <cell><m>\displaystyle \int_{$b}^{$c} g(x) \, dx = $S</m></cell>
  </row>
</tabular>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        <m>\displaystyle \int_{$a}^{$c} f(x) \, dx = </m><answer>$P + $Q</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <m>\displaystyle \int_{$c}^{$a} g(x) \, dx = </m><answer>-($R + $S)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <m>\displaystyle \int_{$b}^{$c} ($k f(x) - $m g(x)) \, dx = </m><answer>$k*$Q - $m*$S</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <m>\displaystyle \int_{$a}^{$b} ($m - $k g(x)) \, dx = </m><answer>$m($b-$a) - $k*$R</answer>
      </p>
    </li>    
    <li>
      <p>
        If <m>h(x) = f(x) + g(x)</m>, the average value of <m>h(x)</m> on <m>[$a,$c]</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>h_{\small{\text{AVG}<m>[$a,$c]</m>}} = </m><answer>1/($c-$a)*($P + $Q + $R + $S)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>   
  </ol>
</p>